{
  "_comment": [
    "Copy to local.settings.json (gitignored) to run the Function App locally",
    "with VS Code / Core Tools. Not needed for `python tools/run_local.py` or",
    "`pytest`, which need no Azure at all - only the local-host / deployed path",
    "reads any of this.",
    "",
    "In Azure these same names are App settings: Function App -> Settings ->",
    "Environment variables -> App settings. Keeping this file in sync with the",
    "portal (add here, add there) is the whole point of listing every one.",
    "",
    "IDENTITY-BASED SETTINGS (the __fullyQualifiedNamespace / __credential",
    "pairs) are never a secret - there is nothing here to rotate or leak. They",
    "authenticate as whoever is SIGNED IN: in Azure that's the Function App's",
    "managed identity; running this locally it's your own `az login` / VS Code",
    "Azure sign-in. For a local run against real Azure resources to work, YOUR",
    "identity needs the same roles the managed identity has - Storage Blob",
    "Data Contributor on the storage account, Azure Event Hubs Data Receiver on",
    "each namespace below. See docs/poc.md and docs/adding-a-log-source.md.",
    "",
    "AZURE_CLIENT_ID picks WHICH identity that is, and is REQUIRED whenever the",
    "Function App's identity is user-assigned rather than system-assigned -",
    "with no system-assigned identity there is nothing to fall back to, so",
    "leaving it empty fails every Azure call with `DefaultAzureCredential failed",
    "to retrieve a token`. Leave it empty for system-assigned (the usual case),",
    "and empty locally, where `az login` is the identity. Its value is the",
    "managed identity's Client ID - Function App -> Settings -> Identity ->",
    "User assigned -> the identity -> Overview. Not a secret.",
    "",
    "AZURE_CLIENT_ID covers this app's OWN Azure calls (the bundle, the output",
    "blob, Redis). It does NOT reach the Event Hub triggers: those are the",
    "host's, and the host takes the identity per connection, so a user-assigned",
    "setup needs `EVENTHUB_<NAMESPACE>__clientId` set to the SAME client id",
    "alongside the pair below - and `AzureWebJobsStorage__clientId` too, if that",
    "connection is identity-based. Fixing only AZURE_CLIENT_ID gets /health to",
    "200 while every trigger stays silent, which reads as two separate faults.",
    "",
    "That error lists every credential type it tried, and the ones that can",
    "never apply here (EnvironmentCredential, WorkloadIdentityCredential -",
    "`missing tenant id, client id, token file path`) always report missing",
    "variables, working or not. Read the ManagedIdentityCredential line; the",
    "others are noise. /health -> `identity` reports both facts directly.",
    "",
    "One EVENTHUB_<NAMESPACE> pair per `namespace:` in config/sources.yaml -",
    "the name is derived (EVENTHUB_ + the namespace, uppercased), never typed",
    "by a source. Adding a namespace there means adding its pair here too.",
    "",
    "DAC_* vs OUTPUT_*: two independent blob destinations, even when (as below)",
    "they happen to live in the SAME storage account. Both take a bare account",
    "URL - https://<account>.blob.core.windows.net, no trailing slash, no",
    "container in it - and the CONTAINER is its own setting: DAC_CONTAINER",
    "(detections IN, default `detections`) and OUTPUT_BLOB_CONTAINER",
    "(signals/alerts OUT, default `pyre-output`). One storage account for both",
    "is just both *_ACCOUNT_URL settings pointing at the same URL, as below.",
    "DAC_LOCAL_DIR is the exception to all of that: a local filesystem path,",
    "read ONLY when DAC_BLOB_ACCOUNT_URL is empty - it's how `pytest` and",
    "`run_local.py` load detections with no Azure at all, and is ignored the",
    "moment DAC_BLOB_ACCOUNT_URL is set to anything."
  ],
  "IsEncrypted": false,
  "Values": {
    "FUNCTIONS_WORKER_RUNTIME": "python",
    "AzureWebJobsStorage": "UseDevelopmentStorage=true",

    "PYRE_ENV": "local",

    "AZURE_CLIENT_ID": "",

    "EVENTHUB_PYRE_EVNTHUB__fullyQualifiedNamespace": "<namespace>.servicebus.windows.net",
    "EVENTHUB_PYRE_EVNTHUB__credential": "managedidentity",

    "DAC_BLOB_ACCOUNT_URL": "https://<account>.blob.core.windows.net",
    "DAC_CONTAINER": "detections",
    "DAC_POINTER": "current.json",
    "DAC_LOCAL_DIR": "./dac",
    "DAC_REFRESH_SECONDS": "30",

    "OUTPUT_HTTP_URL": "",
    "OUTPUT_BLOB_ACCOUNT_URL": "https://<account>.blob.core.windows.net",
    "OUTPUT_BLOB_CONTAINER": "pyre-output",
    "ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL": "",

    "REDIS_HOST": "",
    "REDIS_PORT": "6380",
    "STORM_LIMIT": "1000",

    "AzureFunctionsJobHost__extensions__eventHubs__maxEventBatchSize": "50"
  }
}
